# SAGE125 Captain PR Review & Controlled Merge Workflow

This rule governs how Cursor Agent must behave when the captain (GitHub account
`liuyanbo12`) asks it to review or merge pull requests in
`sage125-ai-scientist-team/SAGE125-AI-Scientist`.

This is a **controlled review-and-merge workflow**, not unconditional auto-merge.
Every gate below must be satisfied before any Approve or Merge action is taken.

## 0. Canonical facts

- Central repository: `sage125-ai-scientist-team/SAGE125-AI-Scientist`
- Captain GitHub account: `liuyanbo12`
- Ordinary teammate PR base branch (the **only** valid target for task PRs):
  `integration/2026-08-10`
- Final release base branch: `main`
- Final release head branch: `integration/2026-08-10`
- Merge method: **squash**, using `--match-head-commit` (never `--admin`, never force push)
- Path ownership source of truth: `docs/governance/task-owner-map.yaml`
- Review policy source of truth: `docs/governance/pr-review-policy.yaml`
- Task content requirements (V3.0): `docs/governance/task-requirements/T01.yaml`–`T09.yaml`
- Content review schema: `docs/governance/schemas/content-review.schema.json`
- Review helper script: `scripts/captain/review_latest_pr.ps1`
- Project-wide Bugbot rules: `.cursor/BUGBOT.md`

## 1. Trigger phrases

When the user (captain) types any of the following (Chinese or English, case-insensitive,
allowing minor rewording), Agent must enter **SAGE125 PR Review Mode**:

- 帮我审核最新的PR
- 审核最新PR
- 检查并处理最新PR
- 重新审核PR #<number>
- 审核PR #<number>
- "review the latest PR" / "review PR #<number>"

Any other phrasing that clearly asks to review/merge a SAGE125 PR should be treated the
same way, but if intent is ambiguous, Agent must ask for clarification rather than guess.

## 2. Definition of "latest PR" when no number is given

When no PR number is specified, "最新 PR" means, in the central repository:

- `state = open`
- `base = integration/2026-08-10`
- sorted by `updatedAt` descending
- the first item in that sorted list

If two or more PRs have effectively the same `updatedAt` (same minute) such that the
"latest" one cannot be uniquely determined, Agent must **not** guess. It must list all
candidate PRs (number, title, author, updatedAt) and stop — no review comment, no merge.

## 3. Mandatory opening report

At the very start of every review, before doing anything else, Agent must output:

- PR number
- Title
- Author
- Draft or Ready for review
- Base branch
- Head branch (and head repository owner, to detect forks)
- Head SHA (this is the SHA that must match at merge time — the "reviewed head SHA")
- Last updated time
- Changed files count
- Additions / deletions
- PR URL

## 4. Base branch policy

- If the PR's base is **not** `integration/2026-08-10` in ordinary review mode:
  - Classify as **P1**.
  - Post review comments explaining the base branch must be
    `integration/2026-08-10`.
  - Do **not** merge.
- A PR with base `main` may only be a **release PR**, and only if **all** of:
  - `head = integration/2026-08-10`
  - Title starts with `[RELEASE]`
  - The captain has explicitly typed:
    `审核最终发布PR并在全部发布门禁通过后合并到main`
  Any other PR targeting `main` must never be auto-approved or auto-merged by the
  ordinary "帮我审核最新的PR" instruction.

## 5. Agent may only review and merge — never edit teammate code

- Agent must never push commits to a teammate's PR branch.
- Agent must never use Bugbot Autofix or any tool to auto-fix a teammate's code.
- All findings go into the GitHub PR as review comments / Request Changes / Approve.
- Teammates fix their own branch and push; the captain (or Agent on the captain's
  instruction) re-reviews after that push.

## 6. Re-review support

- After a teammate pushes new commits to the same PR branch, the captain can say
  "帮我审核最新的PR" again (if it's still the most recently updated open PR against
  `integration/2026-08-10`) or "重新审核PR #<number>" to target it explicitly.
- Each re-review must re-fetch the current head SHA — never reuse a stale SHA from a
  previous review round.

## 7. Reporting discipline

- Every command that is actually executed, and its real result (success/failure/output),
  must be reported accurately.
- Agent must never claim a check, test, or command "passed" if it was not actually run.
- If something could not be run (missing directory, missing tool, permission issue),
  Agent must say so explicitly rather than silently skipping it.

## 8. Where the detailed procedure lives

The full step-by-step review procedure (context gathering, isolated worktree review,
static/semantic checklist, local test matrix per task T01–T09, Bugbot handling, the
merge gate checklist, and the required final output block) is specified in:

- `docs/governance/CURSOR_PR_REVIEW_RUNBOOK.md` (captain-facing operational runbook)
- `.cursor/BUGBOT.md` (project-wide review rules: security, scientific integrity,
  task/path ownership, batch isolation, CI/test integrity, finding format)
- `docs/governance/task-owner-map.yaml` (machine-readable path ownership)
- `docs/governance/pr-review-policy.yaml` (machine-readable merge gate configuration)
- `docs/governance/task-requirements/T0X.yaml` (V3.0 task/wave content requirements)

Agent must read the above before completing a review, in addition to the PR's own
diff, comments, checks, and any task/contract docs the changed paths point to.

## 8b. Two-phase review: engineering + task content (mandatory)

Every review triggered by the phrases in §1 MUST complete BOTH phases:

### Phase 1 — ENGINEERING_COMPLIANCE

Existing gates: base branch, Draft/Ready, head SHA, mergeable/sync, owner paths,
GitHub Checks (never treat skipped/neutral/cancelled/pending/zero as pass), Bugbot
policy, secrets/security, scientific integrity, and local verification commands.

### Phase 2 — CONTENT_COMPLIANCE

1. Identify `task_id` (T01–T09) and `wave` (A/B/C/FREEZE) from, in order:
   PR title → head branch → labels → PR body. On conflict or inability to identify:
   set `CONTENT_COMPLIANCE=WAIT`, request metadata fix, do **not** merge, do **not** guess.
2. Load `docs/governance/task-requirements/T0X.yaml` for that task. If missing:
   `CONTENT_COMPLIANCE=WAIT` / stop.
3. Build a current-wave acceptance matrix from that YAML. Do **not** only inspect
   changed files or trust the PR description as proof of completion.
4. Inspect implementation, tests (including failure paths), artifacts, metrics,
   reproduction commands, contracts, and Wave acceptance evidence.
5. Assign each requirement one of: `PASS` / `FAIL` / `UNVERIFIED` / `DEFERRED` /
   `NOT_APPLICABLE` (definitions in the runbook).
6. Write `content-review.json` **outside** the repo
   (`%TEMP%\sage125-pr-review\pr-<N>-<HEAD_SHA>\content-review.json`).
7. Merge is forbidden unless **both** `ENGINEERING_COMPLIANCE=PASS` and
   `CONTENT_COMPLIANCE=PASS`.

Hard content gates:

- Current-wave `FAIL` → do not merge (`REQUEST_CHANGES`).
- Current-wave blocking `UNVERIFIED` → do not merge.
- Only future-wave gaps may be `DEFERRED` (`allow_future_wave_deferred`).
- Wave C: final Definition of Done must be verified; incomplete → block.
- P2 award-quality recommendations alone do **not** block (`allow_merge_with_p2_only`).
- Screenshots / PR prose / Mock / planned / expected metrics alone never make a
  quantitative threshold `PASS`.
- Never invent metrics or treat teammate claims as evidence.

Every final review report MUST include:

- `ENGINEERING_COMPLIANCE=PASS|FAIL|WAIT`
- `CONTENT_COMPLIANCE=PASS|FAIL|WAIT`
- P0 / P1 / P2 counts
- Blocking requirement IDs (when any)

## 9. Absolute safety constraints (always apply, no exceptions)

1. Never read, print, commit, or modify the real `.env` file.
2. Never print any API key, token, password, private key, or credential value.
3. Never use `git push --force` or `git push --force-with-lease`.
4. Never use `gh pr merge --admin`.
5. Never treat `skipped`, `neutral`, `cancelled`, `pending`, or a missing/zero check as
   passing.
6. Never weaken a PR's checks to make it pass (deleting tests, weakening assertions,
   adding `continue-on-error`, skipping required jobs, renaming jobs to dodge required
   checks, converting failures into successes, or generating empty placeholder
   artifacts).
7. Never modify a teammate's PR branch code.
8. Never merge directly to `main` or `integration/2026-08-10` by pushing — only via
   `gh pr merge` on a reviewed PR.
9. Treat any uncertain merge condition as **not allowed to merge**.
10. Never bypass gates because the captain is a repo admin.
11. Ordinary task PRs may only ever merge into `integration/2026-08-10`.

When in doubt, choose the safer action: comment, request changes, or wait — never merge.
